       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**The problem:** 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg per day. The maximum recommended metformin dose for adults is 2,550 mg per day (some references use 2,000 mg/day for the extended-release form). This order is three times that limit, and it risks severe lactic acidosis.\n\n**What you may have meant:** 2,550 mg is the maximum *total daily* dose. Split three times daily with meals, that is **850 mg per dose**. You may also have meant a lower dose. Metformin is usually started at 500 mg once or twice daily with meals, then increased gradually.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. For example:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or\n- 500 mg PO twice daily with meals (a typical starting dose)\n\nPlease also check the regimen with your resident or attending before it's finalized."
